## ❓ FAQ

**Typecheck fails with `TS2306: File is not a module` after generating.**
When the remote documents expose no `enums*` / `common*` namespaced schemas, the
generator writes an empty `enums/index.ts`, and an empty file is not a module in
TypeScript. `scripts/generate-api.mjs` patches this automatically; if you bypass the
script and call the generator directly, add an `export {};` yourself.

**`pnpm install` complains that esbuild was not built.**
pnpm 10 blocks dependency install scripts by default; esbuild is explicitly allowed via
`pnpm.onlyBuiltDependencies` in `package.json`. If it still fails, run
`pnpm approve-builds`.

**Why does CI not run `pnpm generate`?**
The document endpoint usually lives on an internal network that public runners cannot
reach, so running it would only produce failures unrelated to the code.

**Do consumers have to use pnpm?**
No. pnpm is only this repository's development tool; the published artifact is a plain
npm package that installs fine with `npm`, `yarn` or `bun`.

